{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets","id":711263,"title":"Wood Bullets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T14:53:48-07:00","id":711263,"title":"Wood Bullets","content":"Hello! It's time for a silly question!<br /> I'll go straight to the point: can a wood bullet in the heart send a vampire in torpor just like the canonical wood pole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:05:45-07:00","id":711301,"title":"","content":"In Armory, wooden bullets ranges are halved and suffer a -1 penalty to damage and bullets aren't enough to 'stake' a vampire. In Hunter, Hod rounds are used by Task Force Valkyrie to stake, with the specially crafted wooden bullet shredding into splinters on impact that are enough to consider a vampire 'staked.' As a result, however, firing with them suffer a -2 penalty. Both are first edition books.<br /> <br /> Traditionally people throw Hunter out the window when looking at the other games, but I'd use both systems, with Hunter's variant being a specially made bullet and standard wooden bullets not really crafted to act as a 'stake.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:47:14-07:00","id":711374,"title":"","content":"Wooden bullets are actually a real thing... and are generally used like rubber bullets: crowd control. Shooting someone with a wooden bullet can easily hurt them significantly, but they have trouble penetrating skin; let alone muscle and bone. It's theoretically possible to do something like Hod rounds from Hunter, but if you know you're hunting vampires, just use a modern crossbow with wooden shafted bolts; it's a hell of a lot easier, cheaper, and frankly less suspicious (&quot;I fletch my own bolts with wood instead of buying them,&quot; vs. &quot;I'm using firearms ammunition that is harder to detect with metal detectors... to hunt vampires, not to try to skate around security!&quot;)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T16:41:54-07:00","id":711436,"title":"","content":"It really depends on<i> why</i>, in your canon, stakes do what they do. If it's just any piece of wood in the heart that does it, you're good. But it seems odd to specify a stake if that's the case. It might instead rely on a specific <i>quantity </i>of wood, of which a bullet would likely consist too little to have an effect. Or perhaps it needs to be a solid shaft running from the heart to the outside air, because that somehow short-circuits the vampire's mystic reanimation field.<br /> <br /> The hunter bullets do sort of imply it's the first one, but there's a lot of stuff in hunter that when you try to apply it to a crossover runs into the &quot;but that's not how it works at all&quot; problem, so I'd be hesitant to give them final say on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T19:30:09-07:00","id":711632,"title":"","content":"Myth suggests staking a vampire to the ground keeps them from being able to get up out of their grave. More typically, staking was about releasing gases from the body resulting from decomposition. People of the day didn't understand the phenomenon of body decomposition. A wood bullet is difficult to impart enough force to pierce the heart without going straight through the body, same for any bullet. Given the suspension of belief required to consistently do that, it should be easy enough to do whatever you want. I would suggest penalties to the attempt which can be mitigated by autofire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:25:15-07:00","id":713283,"title":"","content":"For non-bullets, I'm fairly certain the text mentions being able to stake a target using a bow or crossbow, so perhaps a Cho-Ku-No aka Chinese repeating crossbow is an option for rapid fire . . . and maybe I'm just imagining it, but isn't there something somewhere about a shotgun that uses a shell to fire a wooden stake out of the barrel (similar to rifle propelled grenades fixed to the muzzle of a Garand)?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the wood bullet idea is novel, though I still feel like something larger than just a tiny slug of cocobolo or some other hardwood would be needed to make it work\u2014Elfive's comment about a specific quantity to properly stake a Kindred comes to mind\u2014but it is your canon after all.<br /> <br /> The idea of the wood bullet makes me think of someone making use of a really well-crafted tropical hardwood toothpick and a lot of luck, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 10-21-2015, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:36:25-07:00","id":713301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=713283#post713283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of the wood bullet makes me think of someone making use of a really well-crafted tropical hardwood toothpick and a lot of luck, though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Armory book actually mentions loading a shotgun shell with toothpicks, but says it wouldn't work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T18:13:59-07:00","id":713351,"title":"","content":"I haven't read it, but the toothpicks wouldn't penetrate very far into the skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T19:44:48-07:00","id":713514,"title":"","content":"Huh, I missed the shotgun-full-of-toothpicks section, though I was thinking more along the lines of using one by hand as a very, very tiny stake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T20:11:56-07:00","id":713580,"title":"","content":"One thing about Hod rounds. The first is that they're not so much wood as a wooden core in a fiber-like sheath designed to survive piercing the skin and penetrating into the body at a -2 Forearm roll. <br /> <br /> Second, it's mentioned that the rounds are made of mistletoe, so use that as you will if you think it's somehow more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:58:43-07:00","id":734455,"title":"","content":"The shotgun device in H:tV you refer to is called a &quot;zip-stake,&quot; and it doesn't propell the stake throught the air. It's meant to have the barrel placed against the vampire's body, then the shell propells the stake through the heart. With RAW, it's actually more dangerous and less reliable than using a stake by hand, so my group houseruled it to add a shotgun's &quot;damage&quot; to the successes on the attempt. As for ranged staking, try archery. The &quot;Combat Archery&quot; merit in the Hurt Locker previews is amazing (and incredibly similar to a homebrew merit I designed after seeing the Lars Andersen combat archery videos). You really want to go all out, make a deal with a Demon to get a quiver Embedded with In My Pocket, so it never goes empty. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T00:11:04-07:00","id":737203,"title":"","content":"Bah, forget the guns and bows, just chuck a spear at them! One of humanity's oldest inventions, and still the top of the line in vampire stopping power. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T23:19:40-08:00","id":770560,"title":"","content":"Screw wood bullets; just fire the stake out of a gun!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=eKMKtpaq1gE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=eKMKtpaq1gE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=eKMKtpaq1gE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=eKMKtpaq1gE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T10:11:34-08:00","id":770815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=737203#post737203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bah, forget the guns and bows, just chuck a spear at them! One of humanity's oldest inventions, and still the top of the line in vampire stopping power. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>At least use an atlatl in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T12:47:10-08:00","id":770899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=770815#post770815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least use an atlatl in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a fascinating device that is so effective despite the simplicity in structure and design. That said I doubt a modern person could replicate it without great study.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T12:57:33-08:00","id":770902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=770899#post770899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a fascinating device that is so effective despite the simplicity in structure and design. That said I doubt a modern person could replicate it without great study.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be difficult to recreate an authentic one without a great deal of study, but anyone could create a similar assisted-throwing device using the same principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T15:01:52-08:00","id":770979,"title":"","content":"People have done the great deal of study and replicated authentic ones, which has also allowed people to create modernized versions of them.<br /> <br /> You can order them online... (not cheap of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T18:41:03-08:00","id":771121,"title":"","content":"A spear is likely going to be better, unless you're really good with an atlatl. It's the base weapon, a stake in long form. A stick with a point. So simple, but so useful. Grab a spear, stab it through the heart. Is that not working? Stab it everywhere until it dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T01:42:40-08:00","id":771324,"title":"","content":"The advantage of the atlatl is range. It's also easier to achieve surprises from ranged positions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T04:56:30-08:00","id":771397,"title":"","content":"The disadvantage of a spear is it can be hard to hide in a modern setting (I had a group of players have to run from the police because they stole hunting rifles from country ghouls that legitimately owned them, and just brought them into London to look scarier when attacking the chantry). If your characters have the backing of an organisation this is much less of an issue, or if you have a legitimate reason to carry a spear. The advantage of knives and stakes (and pistols) in modern games is that they are easier to hide, although in historical game spears might be passable, depending on era.<br /> <br /> It'll also vary on supernatural. It's a big advantage to be able to transmute a spear or teleport one to your hand on demand. But for vampires and hunters in the modern day a spear will normally be impractical.<br /> <br /> But practicalllity can get in the way of fun, and the latter always comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T07:49:15-08:00","id":771477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=771324#post771324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The advantage of the atlatl is range. It's also easier to achieve surprises from ranged positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also a significant amount of additional force, but I'm not sure that would translate to WoD's combat mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:17:17-08:00","id":771575,"title":"","content":"The disadvantage of an atlatl and a thrown spear is running out of ammo. You throw it, and unless you got a vampire right through the heart or brought a holsterful, now you're standing there with an improvised weapon or bare hands. A spear wielded properly isn't going to be thrown out and lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-22-2015, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T13:58:07-08:00","id":771700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=771477#post771477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a significant amount of additional force, but I'm not sure that would translate to WoD's combat mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe +1 damage, but it's hard to say since purposefully designed atlatl darts aren't great for use as normal spears to compare. I think the bigger mechanical advantage would actually be boosting your throwing range bands. Armor piercing also might be a way to handle the slightly increased force output over raw damage (esp. as a hunting tool first, it was designed to penetrate thick hides).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/711263-wood-bullets?p=771575#post771575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disadvantage of an atlatl and a thrown spear is running out of ammo. You throw it, and unless you got a vampire right through the heart or brought a holsterful, now you're standing there with an improvised weapon or bare hands. A spear wielded properly isn't going to be thrown out and lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's always the risk of range weapons vs. hand to hand weapons.<br /> <br /> Though you also don't have to stand still. Using movement to keep some distance, and having some spare ammo (I mean seriously who travels with a ranged weapon intended for use in violence and only brings one shot unless it's a single fire weapon like some rocket launchers/RPGs?) should let you get 2-3 hits in before getting closed on (unless they have Celerity of course)<br /> <br /> One of the more potent thing about the nWOD combat rules (either edition) is that the damage output per attack is often high enough that ammo is rarely a problem. Unless you're missing a lot, or the target is particularly tough (easier with 2e defense and armor), you don't need a dozen attacks. You usually only need one good one with 2-3 minor ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T18:49:16-08:00","id":771975,"title":"","content":"There's also the concern that a held spear might break or get stuck in something (or a non-heart part of someone). Whether you're throwing it or not, you're only going to get so many attacks out of something that mostly consists of a long stick.<br /> <br /> A spear wouldn't be that easy to conceal, it's true, and although you could come up with any number of clever ways to disguise it, you'd still be carrying around a fairly large object that would tend to make you stand out in a crowd. It would be much easier to conceal it in or on a car, however, so if you're able to tail your target or stake out where they're going to be (no pun intended), then you can just park somewhere nearby and only worry about carrying the weapon when you're going in for the kill. You're probably going to need a way of removing the vampire's comatose body from the scene, anyway, since there's a decent chance that the stake will otherwise get removed before the corpse is exposed to sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T19:38:52-08:00","id":772006,"title":"","content":"An atlatl might break, too. Or it might get full of rot. Or maybe you'll get struck by lightning while holding it. Or maybe your spear is a splinter of the World Tree and Odin will come down and make you One That Never Was at the disrespect you're showing. But in the meantime lets stick within the boundaries of World of Darkness mechanics.<br /> <br /> For one thing, an atlatl and its missiles aren't any easier to hide unless you're talking about a really long spear.<br /> <br /> For another, we're talking about vampires. If you're attacking them with an atlatl if you don't make that stake roll, you're going to be spending another turn reloading. At least with a spear you can make consistent strikes towards the chest, even if you don't make the damage to stake it. Between being able to heal, jump initiative, and automatically reducing lethal damage to bashing and not going unconscious when hit with bashing, you're going to want a one-shot or something that can consistently do a lot of damage.<br /> <br /> As for getting rid of vampire bodies, traditionally vampire hunters would have a large blade to lop off the head once the body is staked. A bottle of lighter fluid and a matchbook might work in its place. You could leave it for the sun if you want but that would be really optimistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}